|~ `::quote`, the kind of code held as a value, its constructor and
   its refusals, the refusal of text read as code, and the verbs of
   quotes. Each resides on `::qlang/quote`, the kind
   whose module declares it; a quote is also the vector of its
   steps, so the verbs of vectors read it as one, and a quote under a
   tag, a link or a snippet of a page, reads them through its shape. ~|

::quote
  |~~ Code as a value, the value of a `~(…)` literal: a vector of steps
      under the code tag. Code is a value so that a verb takes code as its
      slot, `filter`, `sort`, `if`; a page holds laws that run and links
      that lead on; the trail of an error holds the steps it skipped,
      ready to replay; and a query is read, printed and built like any
      data. A literal step is the literal itself; a step that computes is
      a record, `::call`, `::proj`, `::bind` or `::tagged`; `*`, `!|`
      and parentheses wrap their step as `::each`, `::fail` and
      `::group`. `apply` runs a quote on the subject and `parse` prints
      it back. ::link~(::each | doc) ::link~(::call | doc)
      ::link~(::verb | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang | doc :code)

      ~(~(1 | add 1 | mul 2) | count | eq 3)
      ~(~(add 1) | eq ~(add 1))
      ~(~(add 1 | mul 2) | payload | tag ::quote | eq ~(add 1 | mul 2))
      ~(~(add 1 | mul 2) | filter ~(/name | eq :mul) | parse | eq "mul 2")
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/quote}

::QuotePayloadNotVecError
  |~~ `::quote` payload must be a Vec of steps.
      ::link~(::quote | doc)

      ~(
        ::quote{:not :steps}
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::QuotePayloadNotVecError ::map]
       )
  ~~|

::QuoteElementNotStepError
  |~~ Every element of a quote is a step: a literal, a quote, a
      container of steps, or a record or wrapper of code. A value
      with no reading as code, such as a tagged instance of
      another tag, is refused at the index it stands at.
      ::link~(::quote | doc)

      ~(
        [::Box[1]] | tag ::quote
        !| [type /index]
        |  eq [::QuoteElementNotStepError 0]
       )
  ~~|

::ParseError
  |~~ Parser failure — source did not match the grammar.
      ::link~(::quote | doc)

      ~(
        "42 |" | parse
        !| type | spec | /category
        |  eq :parseError
       )
  ~~|

:parse
  |~~ The source text of the quote, the reverse of `parse` on a string.

      ~(~(add 1) | parse | eq "add 1")
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::string | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/parse})

:open
  |~~ The answer of the query the quote holds, run as it stands in the
      scope of the reader, beneath whatever tags stand over it: a link
      opens to the page it names, so `links * open` reads every page a
      page names in one query, and a snippet to the answer it shows.

      ~(|~~ ::link~(1 | add 1) ~~| | links | first | open | eq 2)
      ~(::qlang | doc | links * open | every ~(type | eq ::doc))
      ~(|~~ ::snippet~([3 1 2] | sort) ~~| | snippets | first | open | eq [1 2 3])
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:subject ::quote | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/quoteOpen})
